{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head `2fe99d2f723ea622d62a47f027c779a67419816e`. The press's wait and recovery hold. Two sets of words do not, and both are small to fix. I ran no test at this head, because the findings come from reading the source and sealed evidence. The gate at `ee6e7d1f` stands for what it covers.\n\n## What to change\n\n**1. The new reason tells a person to open a card that is already open.** `apps/views/src/change.ts:246` and `decision.ts:63` build one `reasons` line for every page, and `packages/mcp/browser/main.ts:332` renders `card.reasons` on every page. The sealed `2026-11-01-j2-acceptance-2/out/v3/page-0-item.txt`, line 10, shows that line on the item page at the older code. So a person on the item page, beside **Merge**, reads \"Open this card to read the change, review it or merge it.\"\n\nThe same line also names acts that the card does not offer. `changeActions` returns no action for a merged or closed change, or for a viewer without those grants, and the golden `requested` screen has `actions: []` under these words. This head's own test states the rule: \"A person is not told to do what the card offers no way to do.\"\n\nMake the line depend on what the card shows. For example, the summary says \"Open this card to read the change.\" and adds review or merge only when `actions` offers them, and the item page says only \"The room's rules decide each act.\" `decision.ts` needs the same treatment. The `views-browser.mjs` fixture uses its own reasons, so no script renders these words. Add a test on the projection for at least an item page and a change with no actions.\n\n**2. A superseded read says that it sent nothing after it signed.** `packages/mcp/src/views/session.ts:430` runs `#admit` after the read returns. If the model opens a newer card of that screen during the press, `#active` is false and `#admit` throws \"A newer card replaced this one. Its receipts remain readable; no new act was sent.\" The `read-token` is signed by then. This is older code and a narrow window, by reading only. The request's third item asks the card to say what it knows, and you asked me to press on this check. So fix it here: after the read returns, the words must say that a read was signed and that its answer is not shown.\n\n**While you edit: the digest.** `Lane definition: sha256:…` is now the first line of the body, so it is the first thing that a person reads on the item page. That was the finding in `71d50311` in a new place. Move it to the body's `Rules:` block. The `s4` assertion finds it by line, so it needs no change.\n\n## What I checked, and what holds\n\n**No path repeats a press.** In `act`, the catch reads the view or reopens it, and it never calls `view_act` again. A failure of that read keeps the words and offers **Read the card again**.\n\n**The words about no answer.** Every error that is not an `AppToolError` takes `NO_ANSWER`. That includes \"The app tool returned no readable card data\", where the app did answer. The sentence stays safe, because it claims only that the outcome is unknown, so I do not hold the head for it.\n\n**A stale press signs nothing.** Your claim holds at this head. The cut moves at `session.ts:294`, `:407`, `:490` and `:495`. Each runs in a path that checks `instance.busy` first, and the input path's refresh goes through the same check in `read`. So the second `#admit` cannot answer `stale` during a read. The first runs before signing: `service.ts:695` calls `admit` just before `signedIntent`. The refusal from `#refuseWhileOpen` also comes before signing. `read` and `act` catch every `stale`, so no card shows \"Read it again\". `busy` holds only within one process, so a press on another process is a second press. The words \"Check it before you press again\" cover that case, and custody covers a real act.\n\n**The wait.** I read the request as you did. It asks for a bound that you choose and name, and the recovery makes a longer press safe. A wait of several minutes would only leave the card still for longer. 120 s against the 113 s bound is sound, and the test computes the bound from the constants. The short-wait control fails by the assertion.\n\n**The decision card.** It may drop its definition. The card's actions carry their revisions, and the scope judges each signed act against its own rules, so the digest gave a person nothing to decide with.\n\n**The person's steps.** You did not move them, and the note gives the reason. The planner can overrule that.\n\n**Evidence.** `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-card-press-head/` verifies against `SHA256SUMS` `da472624…` and holds no writable file. The gate exits 0 at `ee6e7d1f`. Run 41341774176 of the card workflow succeeded there. The merge after it touches no card path, so `generated.ts` does not change. The next head changes card paths, so cite a run at that commit.\n\n**Open limit with no owner.** The note says that `decision.ts` still builds the Work list card's summary from a digest and a clause, and it names nobody to change it. `reasonLines` shows that on the `needs-you` screen too. Please name an owner, or ask the planner to.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. A timeout is now a state that the card recovers from, and the server's order decides what a stale press means. The head adds one wait constant and no new server state.\n\n**Security.** No authority changes. The `service.ts` seal moves for one `export`. The defect here is finding 2, a false statement about a signed act.\n\n**Simplification.** The `act` catch is compact, and `readAgain` is the one new flag. I would not reduce it further.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:870c64fe2c59ca812c0c848bf833e6c4898cc7f3","binding":"assigned","head":"2fe99d2f723ea622d62a47f027c779a67419816e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:43abbdec55092c503e3a980c538dcc192d8dc181\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3c7517361fc78a13f67e3f4d0e2c7b5c38a19746\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:368ddc87b427d663ff33feae540bced001b733e1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}